Let \(X\) be a set.  A \emph{metric} on \(X\) is a real-valued function
\[
  d : X \times X \to \mathbb{R}
\]
such that for all \(x,y,z\in X\):
\begin{enumerate}
  \item \(d(x,y)\geq 0\), and \(d(x,y)=0\) if and only if \(x=y\);
  \item \(d(x,y)=d(y,x)\);
  \item \(d(x,z)\leq d(x,y)+d(y,z)\).
\end{enumerate}

